# W2 pins. PostgreSQL, built twice with the reproducibility recipe below.
# repo   https://git.postgresql.org/git/postgresql.git
# FULL 40-hex object ids. A 7-hex prefix is cheap to collide, and the ids
# are fetched from the same remote whose code is then built, so a prefix
# is not a pin.
# older  cce7587<...> (full id below)
# newer  1416f30<...> (full id below; 3 files, 28 insertions)
# recipe ZERO_AR_DATE=1; identical absolute build path and --prefix for both
#        commits (DESTDIR separates the install trees); NO -ffile-prefix-map
#        (PostgreSQL embeds CONFIGURE_ARGS verbatim); -no_uuid NOT used
#        (LC_UUID is content-derived on modern ld64).
# configure flags are part of the dataset definition; see build-w2.sh
